  "source_text": [
    "á-wreón. Take here the passages given under á-wríhan, -wrióhan, dele -wreóhan, -wrióhan, and add: p. -wráh, pl. -wrigon; pp. -wrigen:--Be þǽre deópnysse þe him Drihten áwreáh, Ælfc. T. Grn. 13, 1. Swefne sint gewisse, nelle þú áwreón, Lch. iii. 186, 19. On áwrigenre béc in apocalypsi, An. Ox. 5178. ¶ in the Lindisfarne Gospels the verb means to cover:--Wé áwrigon cooperuimus, Mt. 25, 38. Áwrigon gié operuistis, 43. Áwrigon uelauerunt, Lk. 22, 64. Áwuriáð operite, 23, 30. Áwriá operit, 8, 16. Áwrigen uelatum, 9, 45: opertum, 12, 2. Fore áwrigen obscuratum, 23, 45."
